precept TrafficLight

# A four-way intersection traffic light. The signal cycles Red → Green →
# Yellow → Red under normal demand, with a left-turn phase (FlashingGreen)
# that runs when a left-turn request is pending and a flashing-red emergency
# mode that overrides everything until cleared by an authorized operator.
#
# Vehicles arrive and queue up while the light is red; an Advance event drives
# the cycle. The light refuses to leave red without demand — a side street
# with no waiting vehicles does not interrupt the main flow.
#
# Demonstrates: cross-cutting events (`from any on …`), per-state Advance
# branching, an emergency override that interrupts the normal cycle, and a
# clear-on-exit hook for the emergency reason field.

field VehiclesWaiting as integer default 0 nonnegative
field CycleCount as integer default 0 nonnegative
field LeftTurnQueued as boolean default false
field EmergencyReason as string optional

state Red initial
state FlashingGreen
state Green
state Yellow
state FlashingRed

# EmergencyReason is meaningful only while the emergency override is active.
in Red, FlashingGreen, Green, Yellow omit EmergencyReason
from FlashingRed -> clear EmergencyReason

# Editable window — the operator can adjust the waiting count and queue a
# left-turn while the light is red (e.g. a sensor sync or manual override).
in Red modify VehiclesWaiting, LeftTurnQueued editable

# Events
event Advance
event Emergency(AuthorizedBy as string notempty maxlength 100, Reason as string notempty)
event VehiclesArrive(Count as integer default 1 positive)
event LeftTurnRequest
event ClearEmergency

# ── Transitions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cross-cutting signals — vehicle arrivals and left-turn requests can happen
# in any state without changing the current phase.
from any on VehiclesArrive
    -> set VehiclesWaiting = VehiclesWaiting + VehiclesArrive.Count
    -> no transition
from any on LeftTurnRequest
    -> set LeftTurnQueued = true
    -> no transition

# Emergency override — flips the signal to FlashingRed regardless of state.
from any on Emergency
    -> set EmergencyReason = Emergency.AuthorizedBy + ": " + Emergency.Reason
    -> transition FlashingRed

# Red — advance only when there is demand. A left-turn request takes priority
# over straight-through traffic. With no demand at all, Advance is rejected:
# the signal does not cycle unnecessarily.
from Red on Advance when LeftTurnQueued
    -> set LeftTurnQueued = false
    -> set CycleCount = CycleCount + 1
    -> transition FlashingGreen
from Red on Advance when VehiclesWaiting > 0
    -> set VehiclesWaiting = 0
    -> set CycleCount = CycleCount + 1
    -> transition Green
from Red on Advance
    -> reject "No demand detected — the signal does not advance without queued vehicles or a pending left-turn request"

# Normal cycle through green and yellow back to red.
from FlashingGreen on Advance
    -> set VehiclesWaiting = 0
    -> set CycleCount = CycleCount + 1
    -> transition Green
from Green on Advance
    -> set CycleCount = CycleCount + 1
    -> transition Yellow
from Yellow on Advance
    -> transition Red

# FlashingRed — Advance ticks the cycle counter without leaving the override.
# Only ClearEmergency restores normal operation, dropping EmergencyReason via
# the exit-clear hook above.
from FlashingRed on Advance
    -> set CycleCount = CycleCount + 1
    -> no transition
from FlashingRed on ClearEmergency
    -> transition Red
